class.description:
Each tick, a running task returns [constant RUNNING], [constant SUCCESS] or [constant FAILURE]. Write actions and conditions by extending it and overriding [method _tick]: [codeblock] class_name Chase extends BehaviorTask
@export var speed := 4.0
func _tick(delta: float) -> Status: var target: Node3D = blackboard.get("target") if target == null: return FAILURE var offset: Vector3 = target.global_position - agent.global_position if offset.length() < 1.5: return SUCCESS agent.velocity = offset.normalized() * speed agent.move_and_slide() return RUNNING [/codeblock] Tasks with [member children] (such as [BehaviorSequence] and [BehaviorSelector]) decide which child runs. A running task carries on from where it was on the next tick. A [BehaviorTreePlayer] runs a copy of its tree, so a task's variables belong to one agent. Exported properties are copied from the tree; other variables start fresh.
